  'Post' => '<p>My husband and I contacted Audio Cancun via email while searching for DJ options in Cozumel. &nbsp;They were quick to respond, very professional (asked many key details up front), flexible with our requests and offered a very reasonable price. &nbsp;We mainly wanted them to stick to our pre-determined play list (i.e. we picked all 100+ songs) we wanted to play - but requested that they play the crowd for order, natural breaks, etc. &nbsp;They were able to read our crowd beautifully, had good transitions and we had a blast&#33; &nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>They arrived in good time to run over details prior to our wedding (which we needed since we did not meet them prior to arriving on our cruise ship). &nbsp;They were extremely organized when it came to first dances, announcing the wedding party, toasts, etc.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>*Also, we needed equipment that would keep the dance floor bumping for our 50 person reception in a beach-side palapa. &nbsp;They assured us that their equipment was strong/loud enough and it was -- no complaints at all.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>**Why the 1/2 star off? &nbsp;Unfortunately, one of our guests requested a song with very illicit lyrics be played and cited that the bride and groom said it was okay. Although I don&#39;t fault the DJ for trusting this guest, he could have realized that none of our music had illicit lyrics and double checked with us. &nbsp;We had the song stopped within one verse and there was no harm done <img src="http://www.bestdestinationwedding.com/public/style_emoticons/default/smile.png" class="bbc_emoticon" title=":)" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Overall, I would definitely use Audio Cancun (and our specific DJ was&nbsp;<span style="font-family:Verdana;font-size:13.63636302947998px;">DJ Rockdrigo) -- terrific service and puts on an amazing event&#33;</span></p>
',
  'pros' => 'Professional; Knows how to read a crowd; Great price',
  'cons' => 'None',
